<title>GERMANY: Kohl - Germans should accept little, no wage gains.</title>
<headline>Kohl - Germans should accept little, no wage gains.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Chancellor Helmut Kohl said in a newspaper interview on Wednesday that Germans should accept little or no real wage increases for the next few years in a bid to fight the country's record unemployment.</p>
<p>Kohl also told the Bild newspaper the European currency, set to start in 1999, would give Europe &quot;strong impulses&quot; for growth and that austerity measures to meet criteria to join the euro did not contradict Bonn's fight against unemployment.</p>
</text>
